  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Break-Free – lose your marker while the ball goes round",
  "description": "Half court, one goal with a goalkeeper. A stands in the left corner with the balls, B at the centre line by the left boards, C at the centre line by the right boards and D in the right corner. X defends in front of goal. A passes up to B and moves into the slot. The ball then goes B–C–D, and meanwhile A has to shake off X: go one way, then break into free space just as the ball reaches D. D passes in and A shoots first time. X defends at half pace – stick in the passing lane, but no tackling.\n\nRotation: everyone moves one step in the direction of the ball (A to B, B to C, C to D, D to X and X to the A line). Switch halves after a few minutes.\n\nEasier: without X, focusing only on starting for the shooting spot at the right moment. Harder: X defends for real and D may shoot instead if A is covered. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "A: don't go too early – make your move while the ball is on its way to D."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Change direction sharply so X ends up a step behind."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Move the ball quickly from side to side – then neither X nor the goalkeeper can keep up."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time off the pass."
    }
  ],
